# Copper Linux -- the components starthyprland offers before it starts Hyprland.
#
# Three whitespace-separated columns:
#
#   <name>   <probe>                       <how>
#
# <probe> is a path that exists when the component is present. starthyprland
# installs the missing ones whose <how> is "ingot", by asking ingot
# for them.
# <how> of "image" means this stage already ships it in the ISO: it is
# kept in this list so the report is honest about what a desktop is
# supposed to have, but ingot has no such package and the launcher will
# not try to install one -- a missing "image" component is a broken
# image, said out loud.
#
# The ingot payloads below are drawn from copper-ingot-repo's index, which is
# checked to carry every name listed here. None of them are needed for the
# session to start -- declining the prompt costs nothing and the session runs
# either way -- but they are what turns a bare compositor into a working
# machine. Each payload carries its own dependency closure, so accepting
# downloads several hundred MB; only the ones actually missing are offered, and
# ingot reports each failure without stopping the rest.
#
